PDF bounded zlib adapter

RFC1950 admission, exact raw-body/trailing-data policy and diagnostic taxonomy
are adapted from moonbit-community/flate@0.8.5, revision
3cbcb5c8bde0b34117fd7980b9f41719f2b8f3d7, flate/zlib/zlib.mbt.
Upstream repository: https://github.com/moonbit-community/flate
Upstream license: Apache License, Version 2.0; the complete license is retained
in ../../inflate/LICENSE. Upstream has no separate NOTICE file.

Local changes: shared patched Inflater, explicit conversion budget admission,
physical failed-step output accounting, scope-owned Bytes reservations,
operation-owned scratch leases, incremental Adler32, and a private hard-error
effect that cannot be swallowed by optional PDF resource recovery.

This adapter does not include an upstream compressor, streaming dictionary API,
new backend, or PDF algorithm/lifetime optimization. The existing immutable
compiled-in PDF tables retain their separate initialization path.

Separate local PDF syntax correction: lossless marker EOL preservation,
scalar indirect Length binding and strict source-backed EOL framing selection.
This logic is local project code, not an upstream zlib-wrapper fragment. Every
candidate still uses the unchanged strict bounded RFC1950 adapter and shared
actual-output account; successful repaired data is used by the normal reader.
